<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anscar I of Ivrea</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 902</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Anscar I, Margrave of Ivrea</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anscar I was a Burgundian noble who supported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guy-iii-of-spoleto">Guy of Spoleto</a>'s bid for the crowns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in 888. Guy rewarded him with a march around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivrea">Ivrea</a> in north-western Italy, guarding the Alpine passes. He founded the Anscarid dynasty, whose members included his grandson Berengar II, King of Italy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anscar-i-of-ivrea.jpg" alt="Anscar I of Ivrea" width="320" height="517" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Emanuel Tesauro · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Atto_Anscario.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
